
1) Pull the image

docker pull zzq5233/slambook2-gaoxiang:latest

2) (Optional) Prepare a working folder on your host

Put your SLAMBook2 code/data here so it’s visible inside the container:

mkdir -p ~/SLAMBook2


If you need GUI windows (OpenCV, Pangolin, etc.)
A) X11 (most common)

Allow local Docker to use your X server (host):

xhost +local:docker

the output like: xhost +local:docker non-network local connections being added to access control list



3) Basic run (terminal only)


docker run --rm -it \
  --env DISPLAY=$DISPLAY \
  --env QT_X11_NO_MITSHM=1 \
  -v /tmp/.X11-unix:/tmp/.X11-unix \
  -v /media/mohamed/Transcend_2/3D\ Computer\ Vision/Visual_SLAM:/workspace \
  -w /workspace \
  --name slambook2 \
  zzq5233/slambook2-gaoxiang:latest bash
  
  
  
  
  
  docker run --rm -it \
  --env DISPLAY=$DISPLAY \
  --env QT_X11_NO_MITSHM=1 \
  -v /tmp/.X11-unix:/tmp/.X11-unix \
  -v "/media/mohamed/Transcend_2/3D Computer Vision/Visual_SLAM":/workspace \
  -w /workspace \
  --name slambook2 \
  zzq5233/slambook2-gaoxiang:latest bash
  


You’ll drop into a bash shell inside the container with /workspace mapped to ~/SLAMBook2 on your host.


1) Get the SLAMBook2 code (if it isn’t already in the image)

Inside the container:

cd /workspace
git clone https://github.com/gaoxiang12/slambook2.git


2) Quick smoke test (Chapter 3 tiny demos)
cd /workspace/slambook2/ch3/geometry
mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
make -j$(nproc)
# run a couple of small tests
./useEigen
./coordinateTransform


